{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Archimedean"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation.bounded_degree_saturates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation.bounded_degree_saturates","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSaturation.lean#L127-L132","doc":"**Bounded-degree coordination saturates:** the per-nucleon binding is the\nsame at every `A ≥ 1` — a finite `B/A` plateau, the observed behaviour. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation.perNucleonBounded_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation.perNucleonBounded_eq","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSaturation.lean#L117-L125","doc":"The bounded-degree per-nucleon binding is `ε·k/2`, independent of `A`\n(for `A ≥ 1`). The `A` cancels — this is genuine saturation, not a\ndefinitional constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation.perNucleonBounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation.perNucleonBounded","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSaturation.lean#L111-L115","doc":"Per-nucleon binding under **bounded-degree-`k`** coordination (each nucleon\nbonded to a fixed `k` neighbours; handshake ⇒ `k·A/2` bonds):\n`B/A = ε·(k·A)/2 / A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation.complete_graph_no_saturation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation.complete_graph_no_saturation","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSaturation.lean#L91-L109","doc":"**Complete-graph coordination cannot saturate.** For `ε > 0` the per-nucleon\nbinding exceeds every bound `B` at large enough `A` — no finite `B/A` plateau\nexists. This is the structural reason the complete-graph `z = A−1` (bond count\n`C(A,2)`) is refuted for heavy `A`: it predicts unbounded per-nucleon binding.\n(Qualitative source: `bk-coordination-multiplicity.md`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation.perNucleonComplete_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation.perNucleonComplete_eq","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSaturation.lean#L82-L89","doc":"Closed form: for `A ≥ 1`, `perNucleonComplete ε A = ε·(A−1)/2`\n(because `C(A,2) = A(A−1)/2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation.perNucleonComplete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation.perNucleonComplete","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSaturation.lean#L79-L80","doc":"Per-nucleon binding under **complete-graph** coordination: `B/A = ε·C(A,2)/A`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}